  "body": "`state_default` defines the power level required to send state events:\r\n\r\n> `state_default`\r\n>\r\n> The default level required to send state events. Can be overridden by the events key. Defaults to 50 if unspecified.\r\n>\r\n> *-- https://spec.matrix.org/v1.1/client-server-api/#mroompower_levels*\r\n\r\n\r\nYet, with a power-level of `0`, I can send a `m.room.member` state event when the `state_key` matches my own MXID and is a [valid](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.1/client-server-api/#mroommember) [transition](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.1/client-server-api/#room-membership).\r\n\r\nBut I can't send other state events even when the `state_key` matches my own MXID (403 forbidden, `Denying new event ... because 403: You don't have permission to post that to the room. user_level (0) < send_level (50)`)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nOther related spot in the docs:\r\n\r\n> State keys starting with an @ are reserved for referencing user IDs, such as room members. With the exception of a few events, state events set with a given user’s ID as the state key MUST only be set by that user.\r\n>\r\n> https://spec.matrix.org/v1.1/client-server-api/#state-event-fields\r\n\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\n\r\nI assume `m.room.member` is a special case here but I can't find any docs explicitly calling out that it should be allowed regardless of what `state_default` is set as.\r\n\r\n",
